  "description": "A contemporary adult romance between Elena Marchetti, a 34-year-old Italian-American architect in Chicago, and Marcus Reid, a 38-year-old Black British jazz pianist. They meet at a rain-soaked hotel bar in New Orleans during a storm that strands them; sharp banter over whisky and piano turns into a charged, slow-burn attraction across one electric weekend. Heavy on witty, flirtatious dialogue and simmering tension, with mature romantic and sexual content.",
